--   Moving the collected output onto stack `0` (`outLoop_runs`)
-- statement:
--   Moving the collected output onto stack `0`.
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.J6SegILSlab4`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem J6Seg.Slab.outLoop_runs (s : IState HS) (G : Fin HS → List ℤ) (hA : G lA = []) (hC : G lC = [])
--       (hD : G lD = []) (C CU OP ARG : List ℤ) (o : List ℤ) {LT : List ℤ}
--       (hT : G rTOT = (o.length : ℤ) :: LT) {Bo : ℕ} (hBo : ∀ y ∈ o, zsz y ≤ Bo) :
--       IRuns I iprog (rptX rTOT lA lC lD (.op (.mv rACC 0)))
--         (encK s (skS G C CU OP ARG o.reverse))
--         (encK s (skS (update G 0 (o ++ G 0)) C CU OP ARG []))
--         ((o.length + 1) * (2 * moveCost Bo + 19 + 3000))
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** B-line IL, B1 (streaming slab pass) §4: the whole pass (generic lanes)
--
--   `passP = rptX rNB blockP; rptX rTOT (mv rACC 0)`: the blocks, then the output (collected
--   reversed on `rACC`) is moved onto stack `0`. **`pass_runs`**: from the lane state with the input
--   `xs` (`pre` blocks of `n` slabs of `m` units) the output `passOut … ++ G 0` lands on stack `0`; all
--   skeleton registers are restored (`rACC` empty again). **`passOut_eq`**: for the control list
--   `ctlOf n n' src argOf` of a monotone source, `passOut` is `slabPass` (block form).
